# ── EAS Build archive ignore (repo root) ─────────────────────────────────────
# EAS archives the whole git repository from this root, then builds the app in
# mobile/. The iOS build only needs mobile/, so everything else is excluded here
# to keep the upload under EAS's 2 GB limit. (A .easignore inside mobile/ is NOT
# read, because EAS archives from the repo root — this file is the one that counts.)

# Dependencies (EAS reinstalls these)
node_modules/

# Large sibling content not used by the mobile build
/output/
/downloads/
/scratch/
/web-dist/
/.firebase/
/dist/
/handsoff.md

# Web app source — the mobile app is fully self-contained in mobile/
/src/
/public/
/index.html
/vite.config.*

# Mobile native build artifacts (regenerated by EAS prebuild / pod install)
mobile/android/
mobile/ios/Pods/
mobile/ios/build/
mobile/.expo/
mobile/dist/
mobile/*.aab
mobile/*.apk

# Misc
.DS_Store
*.log
